sycl: reorder NVFP4 expert weights into [qs][d] for the MoE GEMV and the grouped GEMMs

HomeBrain patch on ggml-sycl. Applies on top of 0019.
Upstream tracking: https://github.com/ggml-org/llama.cpp/issues/32757

NVFP4 experts join the lazy per-expert reorder that MXFP4 and the K-quants
use: each expert's 32-byte code blocks first, then its 4-byte UE4M3 scale
groups. The MoE mat-vec reads 16 code bytes with one 16-byte load, the
joint_matrix GEMM stages from the split layout, and the ESIMD GEMM reads the
codes through 2D block loads. B60, 128 experts top-8 [768 x 2048],
test-backend-ops perf: unchanged at 1 token (23.2 vs 23.6 us), 744 -> 711 us
at 32 tokens and 1275 -> 1192 us at 512.

